# NICAI Constitutional Runtime — Runtime Evidence

## 1. Purpose

This directory contains evidence describing the execution state and runtime behaviour of the NICAI Constitutional Runtime.

The purpose of this evidence is to establish that the runtime:

* starts through a defined runtime entrypoint;
* executes within the NICAI runtime boundary;
* preserves `trace_id` across execution;
* exposes defined runtime contracts;
* produces observable execution state;
* supports deterministic execution;
* supports replay and audit evidence;
* maintains explicit ownership boundaries;
* does not silently execute external decisions.

This evidence is intended for engineering review, integration review, constitutional review, and production handover.

