# 6. Runtime State Model

The runtime lifecycle is represented conceptually as:

```text
CREATED
   ↓
INITIALISING
   ↓
READY
   ↓
PROCESSING
   ↓
COMPLETED
```

Failure states are:

```text
INITIALISING
      ↓
   FAILED
```

and:

```text
PROCESSING
      ↓
   FAILED
```

Recovery may return the runtime to:

```text
FAILED
  ↓
RECOVERING
  ↓
READY
```

A runtime must not report `READY` while required runtime dependencies are unavailable.

