# 11. Deterministic Execution

NICAI follows the deterministic execution principle:

```text
Same Input
    +
Same Configuration
    +
Same Contract Version
    +
Same Runtime Version
    =
Same Expected Output
```

Deterministic behaviour is required for replayability and auditability.

Runtime-generated timestamps, identifiers, telemetry values, or environment-dependent fields must be treated as runtime metadata rather than evidence of nondeterministic intelligence logic.

